WEBVTT

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:14.740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:05.180
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.581
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

00:00:06.581 --> 00:00:07.649
(Scenes with child actors
followed production guidelines.)

00:00:07.682 --> 00:00:09.251
Please reconsider, Mr. Seong.

00:00:09.251 --> 00:00:11.686
We have nothing right now.

00:00:23.932 --> 00:00:24.966
My name is Seong Tae Hun.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.602
I fought my way here
by taking on one guy at a time.

00:00:29.337 --> 00:00:30.539
For the past 25 years,

00:00:31.306 --> 00:00:32.741
I bet my entire life...

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:35.310
on this.

00:00:38.447 --> 00:00:39.347
Mr. Seong.

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:49.925
(Director's Office)

00:00:57.365 --> 00:00:59.701
Napa cabbage.

00:01:04.973 --> 00:01:05.874
I...

00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:08.176
Hey, Mr. Seong.

00:01:08.844 --> 00:01:11.780
I was just climbing over
Cheonwang Peak on Jirisan.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.417
At this rate, my heart's going
to hike to heaven before I do.

00:01:16.418 --> 00:01:17.786
I told you already, sir.

00:01:18.186 --> 00:01:20.255
This napa cabbage...

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:23.024
The raw ingredient, napa cabbage,
is the problem.

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.394
Every time, the origin
of the main ingredient changes,

00:01:25.394 --> 00:01:27.129
so the taste of our kimchi
changes completely.

00:01:27.129 --> 00:01:29.464
So how are we supposed to build
loyal customers?

00:01:47.716 --> 00:01:48.650
Right.

00:01:48.884 --> 00:01:50.652
So when we think of napa cabbage,
who comes to mind?

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:51.686
Pardon?

00:01:51.686 --> 00:01:54.289
You, the napa cabbage expert,
are right here.

00:01:54.756 --> 00:01:56.425
I forgot about that.

00:01:57.392 --> 00:01:59.327
Then it's settled.

00:02:00.395 --> 00:02:03.198
So you'll review the sourcing issue again?

00:02:03.198 --> 00:02:04.332
Of course.

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:07.102
You'll do anything for
Mat Story's napa cabbage, right?

00:02:07.369 --> 00:02:08.303
Of course, sir.

00:02:08.637 --> 00:02:11.807
I've spent over 20 years
researching napa cabbage at Mat Story.

00:02:12.307 --> 00:02:15.644
I'll do whatever it takes
to solve this sourcing issue.

00:02:15.644 --> 00:02:17.679
The napa cabbage
that you've been dreaming of...

00:02:18.146 --> 00:02:18.980
I...

00:02:19.581 --> 00:02:22.184
I'll make sure you get it.

00:02:22.184 --> 00:02:23.985
Then this time,

00:02:24.586 --> 00:02:25.854
please make sure you solve it.

00:02:28.457 --> 00:02:29.424
Please work hard on it.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.361
Work hard?

00:02:36.598 --> 00:02:38.133
You're the one who'll be doing
all the hard work.

00:02:40.502 --> 00:02:41.369
The real...

00:02:43.271 --> 00:02:44.573
hard work.

00:03:17.172 --> 00:03:21.243
(Jeongseong Kimchi, Baekseonjang Kimchi)

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.059
I miss you, Daddy.

00:03:37.726 --> 00:03:40.262
You worked very hard today, honey.

00:03:43.131 --> 00:03:46.301
It must be morning
in Toronto right now, right?

00:04:12.194 --> 00:04:14.796
(Mat Story)

00:04:21.036 --> 00:04:21.870
My goodness.

00:04:23.505 --> 00:04:24.673
Look at the HR announcement.

00:04:26.475 --> 00:04:27.442
Next Monday?

00:04:28.176 --> 00:04:29.711
Wow. That's really sudden.

00:04:30.278 --> 00:04:32.214
This is what happens
when you don't have connections.

00:04:33.115 --> 00:04:35.150
So where is this Yeonri-ri branch?

00:04:35.784 --> 00:04:37.119
Don't you know?

00:04:37.119 --> 00:04:40.055
They call it a branch,
but it's basically exile.

00:04:44.693 --> 00:04:46.395
I'll be getting off here.

00:04:46.395 --> 00:04:47.262
Sure.

00:04:49.464 --> 00:04:51.466
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:54.002
Sure. Be sorry.

00:05:31.673 --> 00:05:33.442
(Seong Tae Hun
New Business Department Manager)

00:05:33.442 --> 00:05:34.843
(Transfer Order to Yeonri-ri)

00:05:49.658 --> 00:05:52.561
(Director's Office)

00:06:10.178 --> 00:06:11.947
Let's not just talk about golf.

00:06:23.625 --> 00:06:24.793
Mr. Seong.

00:06:24.793 --> 00:06:26.828
I was just about to call you in
to congratulate you.

00:06:28.563 --> 00:06:29.464
Mr. Choi.

00:06:29.664 --> 00:06:31.133
Members of the board.

00:06:31.967 --> 00:06:35.070
This is the man leading
the napa cabbage revolution.

00:06:35.604 --> 00:06:38.774
Manager Seong Tae Hun
of the Yeonri-ri Branch.

00:06:39.775 --> 00:06:41.676
Let me tell you about this man.

00:06:41.676 --> 00:06:44.012
"I will do anything for the company."

00:06:44.012 --> 00:06:45.247
Thanks to him,

00:06:45.247 --> 00:06:47.416
and his willingness
to work hard for Mat Story,

00:06:49.584 --> 00:06:51.386
I was able to make
this wonderful decision today.

00:06:52.387 --> 00:06:53.422
Everyone.

00:06:53.422 --> 00:06:56.525
Please give a round of applause
for Mr. Seong.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.199
He's factory staff now?

00:07:04.199 --> 00:07:05.133
Sounds great.

00:07:05.133 --> 00:07:06.568
Mr. Choi.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.472
Could I speak with you?

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.375
What is it, Mr. Seong?

00:07:13.642 --> 00:07:15.077
Is there a problem?

00:07:16.078 --> 00:07:19.014
Mr. Choi. Yeonri-ri?

00:07:19.014 --> 00:07:20.115
This...

00:07:20.515 --> 00:07:22.050
isn't right.

00:07:22.551 --> 00:07:24.619
Isn't this what you wanted?

00:07:25.153 --> 00:07:26.755
You said napa cabbage was important.

00:07:27.189 --> 00:07:29.958
If the inconsistent suppliers
are the problem,

00:07:30.258 --> 00:07:31.560
then we should just...

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:35.030
create our own exclusive source
to ensure consistency.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:36.064
But...

00:07:36.598 --> 00:07:38.333
Mr. Choi.

00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:40.268
You're not sending me to Gyeonggi-do
where there's a smart farm.

00:07:40.268 --> 00:07:43.071
You're sending me to Yeonri-ri,
where there isn't even a research team.

00:07:44.139 --> 00:07:46.475
I know what that means.

00:07:49.511 --> 00:07:51.413
Come on. If you know...

00:07:52.481 --> 00:07:53.548
Pardon?

00:07:53.548 --> 00:07:55.951
The company needs you there.

00:07:55.951 --> 00:07:57.352
Are you refusing to go?

00:08:00.689 --> 00:08:02.023
Are you going to resign?

00:08:03.892 --> 00:08:04.693
I...

00:08:05.794 --> 00:08:06.728
I...

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.265
I'm giving you a great opportunity here.

00:08:11.666 --> 00:08:13.034
Whether you take it,

00:08:13.935 --> 00:08:15.637
or not...

00:08:16.938 --> 00:08:18.373
That's up to you.

00:08:19.608 --> 00:08:20.442
But...

00:08:20.976 --> 00:08:21.843
Sir...

00:08:45.801 --> 00:08:49.438
(Resignation Letter)

00:09:15.564 --> 00:09:16.598
Ji Cheon...

00:09:18.133 --> 00:09:20.502
He has to finish med school
and open a clinic.

00:09:22.204 --> 00:09:24.206
Ji Sang and Ji Gu in Toronto...

00:09:25.507 --> 00:09:26.908
still have to finish their studies.

00:09:30.445 --> 00:09:31.947
And you still call yourself
the head of this family?

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:36.918
Did you even think about us?

00:09:36.918 --> 00:09:39.287
Do you want us all to end up
on the street?

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.191
What have I done?

00:10:01.143 --> 00:10:01.977
What?

00:10:03.445 --> 00:10:04.546
It's okay.

00:10:34.042 --> 00:10:34.876
Yes.

00:10:35.577 --> 00:10:37.446
I gave my 20 years to Mat Story.

00:10:39.081 --> 00:10:40.649
Even if I hate it, I'll do it again.

00:10:42.584 --> 00:10:45.320
I, Seong Tae Hun, won't go down like this.

00:10:49.091 --> 00:10:55.297
(EP 1 - Was I Meant to Become a Farmer?)

00:11:14.149 --> 00:11:15.817
What am I doing here?

00:11:15.817 --> 00:11:16.852
What came over me?

00:11:16.852 --> 00:11:18.720
Have I lost my mind?

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.255
Why did I say something
I didn't have to say?

00:11:20.255 --> 00:11:22.624
You idiot.

00:11:25.293 --> 00:11:26.294
Wait a minute.

00:11:27.062 --> 00:11:29.097
Isn't this what you wanted?

00:11:29.765 --> 00:11:31.333
You said napa cabbage was important.

00:11:33.635 --> 00:11:34.803
Wait a minute. Stop.

00:11:35.837 --> 00:11:37.839
Then I'll just prove it.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.241
Seong Tae Hun napa cabbage.

00:11:39.241 --> 00:11:41.543
Wasn't I going to do this before
retiring anyway?

00:11:49.518 --> 00:11:52.087
(Mat Story Yeonri-ri Branch)

00:11:52.254 --> 00:11:54.089
This place is a dump. Darn it.

00:12:24.086 --> 00:12:25.921
Napa cabbage and people have
something in common.

00:12:26.755 --> 00:12:27.889
There are people that you just know...

00:12:27.889 --> 00:12:31.827
you shouldn't mess with.

00:12:31.827 --> 00:12:33.128
the moment you meet them.

00:12:34.196 --> 00:12:35.664
(Yeonri-ri)

00:12:39.634 --> 00:12:41.236
A crime-free village.

00:12:41.636 --> 00:12:43.138
This is Yeonri-ri.

00:12:44.106 --> 00:12:45.107
Welcome.

00:12:53.448 --> 00:12:54.549
Are you from Seoul?

00:12:55.083 --> 00:12:56.785
What are you doing here on this hot day?

00:12:57.586 --> 00:13:00.389
Oh. I'm from Mat Story.

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:02.524
Mat Story?

00:13:04.192 --> 00:13:05.560
What's this now?

00:13:05.994 --> 00:13:06.828
Pardon?

00:13:07.295 --> 00:13:08.530
You got transferred here?

00:13:08.997 --> 00:13:09.931
Yes.

00:13:10.265 --> 00:13:12.467
Are you a resident here?

00:13:12.467 --> 00:13:13.602
I'm the village chief here.

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:16.371
The village chief.

00:13:16.938 --> 00:13:19.307
I'm looking for a place to stay nearby.

00:13:19.307 --> 00:13:21.043
Which real estate office should I go to?

00:13:23.678 --> 00:13:26.081
You're incredibly lucky...

00:13:26.081 --> 00:13:28.417
to have run into me at the perfect time.

00:13:28.917 --> 00:13:31.019
Nothing works in this village without me.

00:13:31.019 --> 00:13:32.554
(Yeonri-ri)

00:13:32.554 --> 00:13:35.791
I'm moving here by myself,
so I don't need a big place.

00:13:36.425 --> 00:13:38.226
Your wife must be thrilled.

00:13:38.226 --> 00:13:40.062
Seeing each other only on weekends
is a blessing, right?

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:44.466
My wife and kids are overseas.

00:13:44.466 --> 00:13:46.768
You're a free bird.

00:13:46.768 --> 00:13:48.837
You flew and ended up here?

00:13:50.005 --> 00:13:51.106
Yeah.

00:13:51.106 --> 00:13:53.909
I guess you are taking a break
for a little bit.

00:13:53.909 --> 00:13:54.976
Who knows?

00:13:55.777 --> 00:13:57.512
You might go back up to Seoul soon.

00:13:58.613 --> 00:13:59.715
Would you like to start with that house?

00:14:07.622 --> 00:14:09.558
You don't see yards like this
in Seoul, right?

00:14:10.292 --> 00:14:12.561
Are you sure this is a yard?

00:14:13.061 --> 00:14:14.196
This house is...

00:14:14.196 --> 00:14:15.097
No thanks.

00:14:19.534 --> 00:14:21.369
I don't think you can call this a house.

00:14:23.138 --> 00:14:25.807
These days, everything is full option.
Did you look thoroughly?

00:14:26.842 --> 00:14:29.344
Yes, full option.
But it's more like negative features?

00:14:30.512 --> 00:14:31.646
Are you sure you came to live here?

00:14:32.347 --> 00:14:33.548
Maybe you didn't come to live here.

00:14:36.618 --> 00:14:38.854
This house has
the highest ceiling in Yeonri-ri.

00:14:38.854 --> 00:14:41.089
Yes, according to your standards.

00:14:41.089 --> 00:14:42.023
My standards?

00:14:43.658 --> 00:14:44.593
You're tall.

00:14:45.227 --> 00:14:48.130
It's so hot.
How long are you going to keep looking?

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:48.964
It's nice and clean, right?

00:14:54.069 --> 00:14:55.971
Those chickens are a bonus.

00:14:56.872 --> 00:14:58.940
I'm not eating chicken starting today.

00:15:03.912 --> 00:15:04.913
This is the last house.

00:15:04.913 --> 00:15:06.848
They're all in about the same condition.

00:15:07.582 --> 00:15:10.285
But this is the best one so far.

00:15:10.285 --> 00:15:12.821
Can we sign a contract today?

00:15:12.821 --> 00:15:14.322
I'll ask.

00:15:19.461 --> 00:15:21.096
He likes Man Sik's place.

00:15:21.096 --> 00:15:22.164
This is the best one so far.

00:15:22.164 --> 00:15:22.998
What?

00:15:23.698 --> 00:15:25.534
- Really? All right.
- There's no time.

00:15:26.068 --> 00:15:27.769
Gosh. I'm sorry.

00:15:27.769 --> 00:15:29.771
There's a lien on the house,

00:15:29.771 --> 00:15:31.173
so it can't be rented.

00:15:31.807 --> 00:15:34.543
It looks like someone
caused trouble again.

00:15:34.543 --> 00:15:36.578
I have an appointment today
that I must get to.

00:15:36.578 --> 00:15:37.312
Then...

00:15:38.146 --> 00:15:40.682
what about this house?

00:15:40.682 --> 00:15:41.917
Yes, that one is available.

00:15:41.917 --> 00:15:44.119
I need to get back now.

00:15:44.119 --> 00:15:45.087
Get going.

00:15:45.087 --> 00:15:46.788
- Thank you. Thank you.
- Good-bye.

00:15:46.788 --> 00:15:48.356
- You know the way out?
- Yes.

00:15:49.357 --> 00:15:51.760
Look at him go.

00:15:52.661 --> 00:15:53.762
Mat Story?

00:15:54.796 --> 00:15:56.364
Goodness. It's so hot.

00:16:06.274 --> 00:16:08.377
If the executive director wants to see me,

00:16:09.544 --> 00:16:11.046
that means it's not over yet.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.215
Let's tough it out.

00:16:13.982 --> 00:16:16.251
Even if I have to grind myself down
like cabbage filling.

00:16:17.052 --> 00:16:18.387
You can do it, Seong Tae Hun.

00:16:23.859 --> 00:16:24.793
Come in.

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:32.734
Did you want to see me?

00:16:36.538 --> 00:16:38.974
About the Yeonri-ri transfer...

00:16:38.974 --> 00:16:41.910
I know that people are gossiping.

00:16:43.779 --> 00:16:46.415
"They sent him to a dead-end post
because he's without connections."

00:16:46.415 --> 00:16:48.316
"It's a trick to push him out."

00:16:50.118 --> 00:16:51.520
Is that what you think, too?

00:16:52.387 --> 00:16:54.156
Sir.

00:16:54.156 --> 00:16:57.292
Please reconsider the Yeonri-ri transfer.

00:16:58.193 --> 00:16:59.061
Yes?

00:17:01.196 --> 00:17:02.564
Not at all, sir.

00:17:03.298 --> 00:17:05.967
I already found a place
to stay in Yeonri-ri today.

00:17:06.868 --> 00:17:08.503
Good. That's the attitude.

00:17:10.739 --> 00:17:12.774
So you have three kids?

00:17:12.774 --> 00:17:14.509
Two are studying in Canada,

00:17:14.509 --> 00:17:15.944
and your eldest is in medical school?

00:17:17.112 --> 00:17:18.880
It must be costing you a fortune.

00:17:19.948 --> 00:17:21.983
How did you know?

00:17:23.985 --> 00:17:27.022
All fathers in Korea live the same life.

00:17:29.691 --> 00:17:31.426
What you'll be doing in Yeonri-ri...

00:17:31.426 --> 00:17:34.029
is much bigger than you think.

00:17:35.297 --> 00:17:37.733
It's a mission that the future of
Mat Story depends on.

00:17:38.734 --> 00:17:42.137
So if I successfully grow
Mat Story napa cabbage,

00:17:42.137 --> 00:17:44.339
does that mean I can return
to headquarters?

00:17:46.274 --> 00:17:47.376
Mr. Seong Tae Hun.

00:17:48.977 --> 00:17:50.078
Go to Yeonri-ri,

00:17:51.012 --> 00:17:53.014
and prove your value.

00:17:55.083 --> 00:17:56.017
Yes, sir.

00:18:06.728 --> 00:18:07.662
I...

00:18:08.697 --> 00:18:10.432
will make a comeback to Seoul.

00:18:11.633 --> 00:18:13.301
Right in the middle of this building,

00:18:13.301 --> 00:18:14.970
I'll put up a napa cabbage statue,

00:18:16.004 --> 00:18:16.838
and my kids,

00:18:18.106 --> 00:18:19.107
and my wife...

00:18:20.208 --> 00:18:22.844
will applaud me as I retire.

00:18:22.844 --> 00:18:24.980
I will do it.

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:53.241
(Wife)

00:18:57.379 --> 00:18:59.281
Honey.

00:19:00.115 --> 00:19:01.116
Well...

00:19:01.883 --> 00:19:03.251
Honey.

00:19:03.251 --> 00:19:05.787
I was just about to call you.

00:19:05.787 --> 00:19:07.489
Where are you right now?

00:19:07.956 --> 00:19:09.324
The call keeps dropping.

00:19:10.292 --> 00:19:11.827
Well, you see...

00:19:12.494 --> 00:19:15.197
I have something to tell you.

00:19:15.197 --> 00:19:18.266
You do? I have something to tell you, too.

00:19:18.967 --> 00:19:20.602
- Oh.
- Door opening.

00:19:20.602 --> 00:19:21.503
By the way...

00:19:22.537 --> 00:19:25.374
Where are you, honey? What?

00:19:27.442 --> 00:19:30.712
Honey, where are you?

00:19:30.712 --> 00:19:31.546
Well...

00:19:36.485 --> 00:19:38.253
What are you doing here, honey?

00:19:38.253 --> 00:19:39.721
You see...

00:19:39.721 --> 00:19:41.857
It just happened, honey.

00:19:47.062 --> 00:19:47.963
Dad.

00:19:50.465 --> 00:19:52.067
You've grown so much.

00:19:52.734 --> 00:19:54.703
Dad, what's with all these boxes?

00:19:56.571 --> 00:19:57.406
Well...

00:19:59.474 --> 00:20:01.543
Are you going somewhere?

00:20:06.314 --> 00:20:07.616
Have you lost your mind?

00:20:08.216 --> 00:20:09.518
A research assignment?

00:20:09.851 --> 00:20:11.386
And in the countryside?

00:20:11.386 --> 00:20:13.555
Why didn't you tell me this sooner?

00:20:13.555 --> 00:20:14.890
You're the one to talk.

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:17.793
What are you doing here with
the kids without telling me?

00:20:17.793 --> 00:20:19.528
I had my reasons.

00:20:19.528 --> 00:20:21.496
Exactly. Why are the kids...

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:23.565
Ji Cheon. What are you doing here?

00:20:24.433 --> 00:20:25.834
Mom told me to come.

00:20:26.401 --> 00:20:28.336
I asked him to come to the airport.

00:20:28.336 --> 00:20:29.805
We had a lot of luggage.

00:20:29.805 --> 00:20:31.440
Exactly. So why?

00:20:34.676 --> 00:20:35.544
Ji Sang...

00:20:36.511 --> 00:20:37.679
was expelled.

00:20:37.679 --> 00:20:38.814
What?

00:20:39.381 --> 00:20:41.216
Expelled?

00:20:41.216 --> 00:20:42.951
There was a fight among some kids...

00:20:42.951 --> 00:20:44.853
It just happened.

00:20:44.853 --> 00:20:46.221
Would you understand even if I told you?

00:20:46.221 --> 00:20:47.889
What kind of fight was it
that you got expelled?

00:20:47.889 --> 00:20:50.258
Seong Ji Sang. Come here right now!

00:20:50.258 --> 00:20:51.660
You can scold him later.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:54.396
Right now, you need to
figure out this situation.

00:20:54.396 --> 00:20:57.365
You should've told me first
if something like this happened.

00:20:57.365 --> 00:20:59.601
Did you ever answer your phone
when I called you?

00:20:59.601 --> 00:21:01.937
When I called you back,
you never answered either.

00:21:01.937 --> 00:21:04.940
I was trying to sort things out.
That's why.

00:21:08.877 --> 00:21:11.146
(Moving Company)

00:21:16.218 --> 00:21:17.919
For now, let's go.

00:21:21.623 --> 00:21:23.458
Where exactly are we going?

00:21:28.063 --> 00:21:31.066
We'll be there in the blink of an eye.

00:21:31.967 --> 00:21:33.235
It's not too far from Seoul.

00:21:37.372 --> 00:21:40.675
(Simwoo-myeon 157 km)

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:56.858
(Moving Day)

00:21:58.994 --> 00:21:59.995
What?

00:22:00.962 --> 00:22:01.863
What?

00:22:03.532 --> 00:22:05.267
A rural vacation?

00:22:06.935 --> 00:22:08.437
A rural vacation?

00:22:08.437 --> 00:22:10.005
This isn't the house.

00:22:10.005 --> 00:22:11.339
I clearly...

00:22:11.339 --> 00:22:13.308
showed him the pictures...

00:22:13.308 --> 00:22:16.578
You rented a house
just by looking at pictures?

00:22:16.578 --> 00:22:20.215
That's not it.
I think there's been a mistake.

00:22:20.215 --> 00:22:21.650
What the...

00:22:22.217 --> 00:22:23.151
Daddy.

00:22:23.151 --> 00:22:24.319
Dad.

00:22:24.886 --> 00:22:26.188
No one can live here.

00:22:26.822 --> 00:22:29.057
Look. It's haunted.

00:22:29.991 --> 00:22:31.359
Haunted?

00:22:31.793 --> 00:22:32.928
Seriously?

00:22:33.428 --> 00:22:34.996
No, Ji Gu. This...

00:22:34.996 --> 00:22:36.064
Unbelievable.

00:22:37.332 --> 00:22:40.635
I clearly asked for this house.

00:22:40.635 --> 00:22:42.104
This one.

00:22:42.704 --> 00:22:44.740
- It's not that.
- Stop.

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:45.874
You're here.

00:22:46.742 --> 00:22:48.477
I thought you were coming alone,
but the whole family is here.

00:22:49.244 --> 00:22:50.645
- Welcome to Yeonri-ri... What?
- Chief.

00:22:52.481 --> 00:22:53.648
This isn't the house.

00:22:54.249 --> 00:22:55.217
What's wrong?

00:22:55.484 --> 00:22:57.352
Well, I...

00:22:57.919 --> 00:23:00.088
I was talking about this house.

00:23:00.789 --> 00:23:01.990
We looked at so many houses.

00:23:01.990 --> 00:23:03.258
How would I know which house is which?

00:23:05.394 --> 00:23:07.729
It's so hot.
How long are you going to keep looking?

00:23:07.729 --> 00:23:09.498
You can take a look.
I won't do it anymore.

00:23:09.831 --> 00:23:11.099
I won't do it. I won't.

00:23:12.033 --> 00:23:13.502
What about this house?

00:23:14.169 --> 00:23:15.270
Yes, that one is available.

00:23:29.317 --> 00:23:30.819
They just got here from Canada.

00:23:30.819 --> 00:23:32.754
How can they live in a place like this?

00:23:33.288 --> 00:23:34.823
Actually, it's perfect.

00:23:34.823 --> 00:23:36.591
That other house has
a broken water pipe right now.

00:23:36.591 --> 00:23:38.293
There's no hot water either.

00:23:38.293 --> 00:23:39.361
This is what we'll do.

00:23:39.728 --> 00:23:40.896
You stay here for now.

00:23:40.896 --> 00:23:42.898
When the repairs are done,
you can move there, okay?

00:23:44.466 --> 00:23:47.369
This place is closer to
the Mat Story field anyway.

00:23:53.008 --> 00:23:54.009
Sir.

00:23:54.609 --> 00:23:56.812
Should we unload your stuff or not?

00:23:56.812 --> 00:23:58.046
It's getting dark.

00:23:59.614 --> 00:24:01.416
Are you going to make your family...

00:24:01.416 --> 00:24:03.518
sleep in the yard tonight? Well?

00:24:15.464 --> 00:24:16.598
Please unload everything.

00:24:16.598 --> 00:24:17.532
He said to unload.

00:24:25.374 --> 00:24:28.377
I'm sure the inside is okay.

00:24:31.480 --> 00:24:32.414
Let's go, Ji Sang.

00:24:45.961 --> 00:24:47.028
Be careful.

00:24:50.098 --> 00:24:51.032
Ugh, dust.

00:24:59.007 --> 00:25:00.542
Be careful, Ji Gu. Be careful.

00:25:00.542 --> 00:25:02.310
Don't run. Don't run. It's dusty.

00:25:02.544 --> 00:25:03.879
No.

00:25:04.546 --> 00:25:05.580
No. Bugs! Bugs!

00:25:05.580 --> 00:25:07.149
I'm going back.
I'm going back to Seoul.

00:25:07.149 --> 00:25:08.316
No, no, no.

00:25:08.316 --> 00:25:09.885
It's dangerous right now. It's nighttime.

00:25:09.885 --> 00:25:11.987
I can clean this place up quickly.
I'll get rid of the cockroaches and...

00:25:11.987 --> 00:25:12.954
Bugs.

00:25:14.456 --> 00:25:16.491
A spider over there.

00:25:19.694 --> 00:25:21.196
You're not supposed to kill spiders.

00:25:21.797 --> 00:25:22.731
They say it brings bad luck.

00:25:26.001 --> 00:25:28.437
Get lost. This is my room.

00:25:28.437 --> 00:25:30.138
No, that's mine.

00:25:30.739 --> 00:25:31.640
Mom.

00:25:31.640 --> 00:25:34.176
Be quiet. I'm exhausted.

00:25:35.243 --> 00:25:36.745
I can't share a room with him.

00:25:36.745 --> 00:25:38.013
I need my own room.

00:25:38.380 --> 00:25:40.882
Me too. He's so dirty.

00:25:40.882 --> 00:25:42.150
He's always dropping snack crumbs.

00:25:43.919 --> 00:25:45.187
You two. Come here.

00:25:45.854 --> 00:25:46.822
Right now.

00:25:47.355 --> 00:25:48.323
Come here.

00:25:50.192 --> 00:25:51.526
That's not fair.

00:25:51.793 --> 00:25:53.528
I want my own room!

00:25:53.528 --> 00:25:54.463
As for the room...

00:25:57.766 --> 00:26:00.068
You have to share a room.
If you don't want to...

00:26:02.971 --> 00:26:03.839
Get out.

00:26:05.374 --> 00:26:06.475
Dad.

00:26:06.842 --> 00:26:09.644
Is your company bankrupt?

00:26:11.380 --> 00:26:12.614
No.

00:26:12.848 --> 00:26:14.516
I came here to do research.

00:26:14.516 --> 00:26:16.418
Development. Yes.

00:26:17.085 --> 00:26:18.053
Development.

00:26:19.154 --> 00:26:20.088
My head.

00:26:29.965 --> 00:26:30.932
Honey.

00:26:31.566 --> 00:26:32.968
Be careful. Are you okay?

00:26:33.969 --> 00:26:35.003
Goodness.

00:26:35.804 --> 00:26:36.838
A little more.

00:26:36.838 --> 00:26:38.340
No. Push. Push.

00:26:38.840 --> 00:26:40.909
No, Ji Cheon. Pull it that way.

00:26:40.909 --> 00:26:41.843
Push.

00:26:41.843 --> 00:26:43.278
Don't push like that. Grab the top.

00:26:43.278 --> 00:26:45.113
Grab the top. Grab the top.

00:26:45.781 --> 00:26:48.650
You have to grab the top.

00:26:50.318 --> 00:26:51.453
I'm sorry, but can you please help?

00:26:52.087 --> 00:26:54.356
You don't have much stuff.
It'll be done soon.

00:26:54.356 --> 00:26:55.857
You can't see anything once the sun sets.

00:26:55.857 --> 00:26:57.392
Finish it up quickly. Come on.

00:26:58.727 --> 00:26:59.661
Finish it up.

00:27:01.897 --> 00:27:03.465
He's no help.

00:27:04.332 --> 00:27:05.700
Slowly. Slowly. Slowly.

00:27:12.474 --> 00:27:13.742
No.

00:27:14.276 --> 00:27:17.179
Are you moving your stuff or
breaking the cart?

00:27:18.180 --> 00:27:20.015
The first one, obviously.

00:27:21.349 --> 00:27:22.417
Keep up the good work.

00:27:26.822 --> 00:27:28.390
- Thank you.
- Bye.

00:27:30.092 --> 00:27:32.427
It won't be delivered tomorrow.
I'm going crazy here.

00:27:32.427 --> 00:27:34.262
Even in Canada, everything gets delivered.

00:27:34.262 --> 00:27:36.164
How am I supposed to live here?

00:27:38.667 --> 00:27:40.836
Was this always this big?

00:27:41.403 --> 00:27:42.237
It...

00:27:42.237 --> 00:27:45.741
By the way, the gas isn't connected.

00:27:45.741 --> 00:27:47.509
Isn't the landlord coming? Where is he?

00:27:48.143 --> 00:27:50.579
- Well...
- Here's the landlady.

00:27:56.651 --> 00:27:58.587
(Deok Rae)

00:28:03.158 --> 00:28:05.060
(Ok Rae)

00:28:07.662 --> 00:28:09.631
(Mak Rae)

00:28:16.071 --> 00:28:19.307
Is this a dining table
or a wooden platform?

00:28:19.307 --> 00:28:21.410
Why is it so big?

00:28:21.410 --> 00:28:24.246
The furniture doesn't match at all.

00:28:24.246 --> 00:28:26.214
How chaotic.

00:28:26.214 --> 00:28:27.816
Are you the landlady?

00:28:28.283 --> 00:28:30.185
I'm Seong Tae Hun, the tenant.

00:28:30.185 --> 00:28:31.219
Not me.

00:28:31.620 --> 00:28:32.487
Her.

00:28:34.289 --> 00:28:35.757
What about the gas?

00:28:35.757 --> 00:28:38.460
You need to call the gas company.
Why are you looking for me?

00:28:38.460 --> 00:28:39.661
Do you want me to fart instead?

00:28:39.661 --> 00:28:42.297
Stop it, Ok Rae.

00:28:42.764 --> 00:28:45.133
You need LPG.

00:28:45.133 --> 00:28:46.668
Take out your phone.

00:28:47.169 --> 00:28:50.205
This is the number you should call.

00:28:51.473 --> 00:28:53.375
- Okay?
- Okay.

00:28:53.375 --> 00:28:55.544
We came by to see how you were doing.

00:28:55.877 --> 00:28:58.480
The whole family is here.

00:28:58.480 --> 00:28:59.681
It's nice and lively.

00:28:59.848 --> 00:29:00.949
Welcome.

00:29:01.316 --> 00:29:03.018
Do you want me to fart for you?

00:29:03.018 --> 00:29:04.720
Ok Rae. Let's go. Let's go.

00:29:11.393 --> 00:29:14.396
(Moving Day)

00:29:38.820 --> 00:29:40.922
I'll be washing the rice until tomorrow.

00:29:42.424 --> 00:29:44.626
How am I supposed to cook
in a place like this?

00:29:48.563 --> 00:29:49.765
Should we eat out today?

00:29:49.765 --> 00:29:51.400
We must eat jajangmyeon on moving day.

00:29:51.400 --> 00:29:53.969
Ji Sang. Ji Gu. It's been a while
since you had jajangmyeon, right?

00:29:53.969 --> 00:29:54.870
Let's go.

00:29:58.940 --> 00:30:00.075
This is jajangmyeon?

00:30:02.511 --> 00:30:05.047
It's cooler now that the wind is blowing.

00:30:07.115 --> 00:30:08.050
It's good.

00:30:09.117 --> 00:30:10.986
Let's eat something even better soon.

00:30:11.420 --> 00:30:12.954
There's no restaurant that delivers here.

00:30:12.954 --> 00:30:15.757
I don't know
if we're eating kimchi for the ramyeon,

00:30:16.258 --> 00:30:18.927
or the other way around.

00:30:19.961 --> 00:30:21.730
It's good when you eat them
together, honey.

00:30:22.564 --> 00:30:24.466
With this,

00:30:27.235 --> 00:30:28.937
that kimchi goes really well.

00:31:06.708 --> 00:31:08.009
Where am I?

00:31:08.009 --> 00:31:09.344
I'll only stay for a few days.

00:31:10.345 --> 00:31:12.381
When did you get here, honey?

00:31:12.381 --> 00:31:15.450
If I left you alone
after seeing this mess,

00:31:15.450 --> 00:31:17.018
I wouldn't be able to sleep. That's why.

00:31:21.323 --> 00:31:23.592
Mom. Mom!

00:31:23.592 --> 00:31:25.160
- What is it? What?
- A centipede.

00:31:25.160 --> 00:31:26.661
Wow. A centipede. It's so gross.

00:31:26.661 --> 00:31:28.730
- A centipede.
- A centipede.

00:31:28.730 --> 00:31:30.198
It's so disgusting.

00:31:30.198 --> 00:31:31.199
A centipede?

00:31:31.533 --> 00:31:34.035
Ji Sang. Go get Ji Cheon,

00:31:34.035 --> 00:31:35.537
and close the door behind you.

00:31:35.537 --> 00:31:38.573
No. You go close it.

00:31:38.974 --> 00:31:40.842
Go now. Go.

00:31:40.842 --> 00:31:43.045
Go close the door now.

00:31:43.678 --> 00:31:45.047
But it's so gross.

00:31:52.788 --> 00:31:54.956
I think my whole body is itchy.

00:31:56.158 --> 00:31:58.560
Maybe we should just sleep here
for tonight.

00:32:02.697 --> 00:32:03.732
Dad.

00:32:03.732 --> 00:32:05.734
- Yes?
- Wake up.

00:32:12.441 --> 00:32:13.942
Mom.

00:32:13.942 --> 00:32:14.843
Yes?

00:32:14.843 --> 00:32:16.311
I'm scared.

00:32:16.311 --> 00:32:18.246
Ji Gu, you're scared?

00:32:18.246 --> 00:32:20.849
I'm scared because all the lights are off.

00:32:22.017 --> 00:32:23.685
It kind of feels like we're camping.

00:32:25.120 --> 00:32:26.088
Actually,

00:32:26.988 --> 00:32:29.725
they say the countryside is much better
for people than the city.

00:32:30.726 --> 00:32:31.993
There's phytoncide from the trees,

00:32:32.627 --> 00:32:34.763
the smell of grass calms your nerves,

00:32:35.564 --> 00:32:37.165
and since there's no noise pollution,

00:32:37.165 --> 00:32:39.768
your body produces more melatonin
so you can sleep deeper.

00:32:40.836 --> 00:32:43.171
Yes, but...

00:32:43.939 --> 00:32:46.942
we should sleep at night, right?

00:32:47.576 --> 00:32:48.510
Okay.

00:32:48.510 --> 00:32:49.578
But I'm scared.

00:32:49.578 --> 00:32:51.079
Let's just hang in there a little longer.

00:32:51.079 --> 00:32:52.514
But I don't want to.

00:32:52.514 --> 00:32:53.415
Good night.

00:32:53.415 --> 00:32:54.516
Oh, my God.

00:32:55.417 --> 00:32:56.918
I can't sleep.

00:32:58.186 --> 00:32:59.554
I'll be up all night.

00:33:17.305 --> 00:33:18.407
You three.

00:33:19.975 --> 00:33:21.143
You've all grown so much.

00:34:55.404 --> 00:34:57.806
Why doesn't this key go in?

00:34:59.841 --> 00:35:00.742
Darn.

00:35:01.109 --> 00:35:03.879
(Mat Story Yeonri-ri Branch)

00:35:38.480 --> 00:35:39.514
What are you doing?

00:35:39.514 --> 00:35:41.216
Who are you? Who?

00:35:57.365 --> 00:36:00.335
Do people in this town
enjoy scaring others?

00:36:01.069 --> 00:36:02.437
Since yesterday...

00:36:03.805 --> 00:36:04.740
It's open.

00:36:07.042 --> 00:36:08.110
Are you the building manager?

00:36:09.344 --> 00:36:10.779
Or a Mat Story employee?

00:36:22.691 --> 00:36:24.292
You'll be able to open most things.

00:36:27.162 --> 00:36:29.131
Wait. Wait...

00:36:32.033 --> 00:36:33.835
So you think I'm the outcast
they sent down here?

00:36:34.102 --> 00:36:35.737
You can look down on me all you want.

00:36:54.423 --> 00:36:57.059
(Napa cabbage research fully suspended)

00:37:11.940 --> 00:37:14.576
How am I supposed to research
napa cabbage in a place like this?

00:37:29.591 --> 00:37:32.027
Napa cabbage research fully suspended?

00:37:44.906 --> 00:37:47.642
I want to go back to Seoul.

00:37:47.642 --> 00:37:49.544
I'm going to kill Director Choi.

00:37:49.544 --> 00:37:51.313
All you Mat Story jerks.

00:37:54.149 --> 00:37:55.250
You abandoned me?

00:37:55.951 --> 00:37:57.085
Me?

00:38:13.568 --> 00:38:15.904
(2016 Work Log)

00:38:18.807 --> 00:38:20.976
The soil has been neglected
for a long time,

00:38:20.976 --> 00:38:24.413
so drainage and nutrients are
completely imbalanced.

00:38:24.413 --> 00:38:26.848
All professional staff
need to be deployed.

00:38:28.016 --> 00:38:29.618
The site selection was a failure.

00:38:33.321 --> 00:38:34.656
What's going to happen now?

00:38:37.926 --> 00:38:39.127
Do nothing.

00:38:40.729 --> 00:38:41.663
Nothing.

00:38:43.665 --> 00:38:45.700
Headquarters has abandoned Yeonri-ri.

00:38:45.700 --> 00:38:47.269
Do nothing.

00:38:48.503 --> 00:38:49.471
Headquarters...

00:38:51.339 --> 00:38:52.941
has abandoned Yeonri-ri.

00:39:31.380 --> 00:39:33.682
Why won't this start?

00:39:43.158 --> 00:39:44.393
Why won't it?

00:39:46.328 --> 00:39:48.563
This is his first day at work.

00:39:50.899 --> 00:39:51.933
It's hot.

00:39:53.235 --> 00:39:54.302
It's hot.

00:39:56.705 --> 00:39:58.006
Air conditioner...

00:40:00.042 --> 00:40:00.976
Come on.

00:40:06.715 --> 00:40:09.084
Is it jet lag? I'm dying.

00:40:12.521 --> 00:40:13.488
It's hot.

00:40:15.824 --> 00:40:19.361
If you're hot, why are you wrapped up
in a blanket?

00:40:19.361 --> 00:40:21.496
Goodness. Look at all this sweat.

00:40:21.496 --> 00:40:22.597
Goodness.

00:40:24.733 --> 00:40:25.567
What?

00:40:26.968 --> 00:40:28.003
Dr. Seong?

00:40:29.137 --> 00:40:30.639
Dr. Seong.

00:40:32.374 --> 00:40:33.442
Dr. Seong?

00:40:37.479 --> 00:40:44.052
(Yeonri-ri Village)

00:40:55.363 --> 00:40:56.331
This is nice.

00:42:02.464 --> 00:42:03.665
Son, where are you?

00:42:03.665 --> 00:42:04.900
You need to eat lunch.

00:42:16.545 --> 00:42:17.345
Move out of the way.

00:42:22.517 --> 00:42:24.753
Don't use your phone while you're walking.
Or you'll get hurt.

00:42:30.058 --> 00:42:31.359
I should go back now.

00:42:49.144 --> 00:42:51.346
What's that? Is that a snail?

00:42:52.114 --> 00:42:54.516
What is he doing in the rice field?

00:43:01.089 --> 00:43:03.692
Your clothes are dirty already.
Come with us.

00:43:05.894 --> 00:43:06.828
Me?

00:43:07.062 --> 00:43:09.498
Who else is there?

00:43:10.065 --> 00:43:13.101
Are we allowed to take him with us?

00:43:13.101 --> 00:43:15.203
He's with that Mat Story family
that caused all that fuss.

00:43:15.203 --> 00:43:18.306
Mat Story or whatever,
we're short on workers.

00:43:18.306 --> 00:43:20.809
Making a guy who's doing nothing
work won't kill him.

00:43:22.310 --> 00:43:23.178
Let's go.

00:43:25.881 --> 00:43:27.349
Together.

00:43:40.162 --> 00:43:41.396
It smells amazing in here.

00:43:41.763 --> 00:43:42.664
Hey.

00:43:43.565 --> 00:43:46.668
Looks like a great harvest this year.

00:43:47.002 --> 00:43:48.503
Look at them hanging everywhere.

00:43:48.503 --> 00:43:49.704
My goodness.

00:43:50.172 --> 00:43:53.742
These cucumbers are smooth
and handsome, just like me.

00:43:54.109 --> 00:43:55.343
Go on in.

00:44:03.151 --> 00:44:04.119
Wow.

00:44:06.722 --> 00:44:08.356
Close your mouth before a fly goes in.

00:44:08.356 --> 00:44:09.458
You've never seen a cucumber field before?

00:44:10.492 --> 00:44:12.794
No, I've never seen a cucumber field
like this.

00:44:13.562 --> 00:44:14.429
Here.

00:44:15.130 --> 00:44:18.900
Take this and start from over there.
Pick as you go.

00:44:19.768 --> 00:44:20.702
Look.

00:44:22.437 --> 00:44:24.272
Like this. Like this.

00:44:28.577 --> 00:44:30.479
If you don't fill this basket,
you won't get paid today.

00:44:31.480 --> 00:44:32.314
Okay.

00:44:33.148 --> 00:44:34.649
What? Wait.

00:44:34.649 --> 00:44:37.018
I've never done this kind of work before.

00:44:39.921 --> 00:44:42.224
You think I was born
picking cucumbers then?

00:44:42.224 --> 00:44:43.425
Do it before I smack you.

00:44:45.527 --> 00:44:46.695
I'll try.

00:44:57.139 --> 00:44:58.707
When am I going to organize all this?

00:45:01.543 --> 00:45:05.147
First, I'll put away the blankets.

00:45:06.948 --> 00:45:08.016
Stationery...

00:45:22.564 --> 00:45:23.432
There.

00:45:23.899 --> 00:45:24.833
Come on.

00:45:25.567 --> 00:45:27.669
My phone.

00:45:27.669 --> 00:45:30.038
I need to call Carol.

00:45:31.206 --> 00:45:32.474
Mom.

00:45:33.608 --> 00:45:36.144
We're going back to Seoul, right?

00:45:36.945 --> 00:45:39.381
Or let's go back to Toronto. Please?

00:45:39.381 --> 00:45:42.384
What would you even do in Toronto?

00:45:43.852 --> 00:45:45.854
Carol says she misses me.

00:45:47.322 --> 00:45:49.624
I even have money to buy a plane ticket.

00:45:50.325 --> 00:45:53.128
So let's go back.

00:45:53.128 --> 00:45:54.529
Is anyone home?

00:45:56.565 --> 00:45:58.500
Hello?

00:45:59.568 --> 00:46:00.569
Yes?

00:46:17.953 --> 00:46:18.954
Who are you?

00:46:19.521 --> 00:46:20.355
Hi.

00:46:20.922 --> 00:46:22.858
You're from Seoul, right?

00:46:25.627 --> 00:46:26.695
Can I help you?

00:46:29.030 --> 00:46:29.931
Well...

00:46:30.465 --> 00:46:34.236
She's the head
of the Yeonri-ri Women's Association.

00:46:34.569 --> 00:46:37.072
She also runs a cafe in town,

00:46:37.072 --> 00:46:38.573
and a hair salon.

00:46:40.108 --> 00:46:41.309
She's the big shot of Yeonri-ri.

00:46:44.246 --> 00:46:45.580
I'm not a big shot.

00:46:46.882 --> 00:46:48.650
I'm Nam Hye Sun.

00:46:49.851 --> 00:46:52.654
I live right across from you.

00:46:54.589 --> 00:46:55.490
I see.

00:46:56.124 --> 00:46:58.160
It's nice to meet you.

00:46:59.861 --> 00:47:02.164
So when are you planning to
go back to Seoul?

00:47:03.365 --> 00:47:05.834
My husband will go back
after he finishes his work.

00:47:06.301 --> 00:47:08.303
But I might go back sooner.

00:47:08.970 --> 00:47:11.640
Those people from Mat Story...

00:47:12.040 --> 00:47:13.742
Did they last two months?

00:47:13.742 --> 00:47:15.110
No.

00:47:15.110 --> 00:47:17.012
The longest lasted a month and a half.

00:47:17.546 --> 00:47:18.980
Oh.

00:47:20.849 --> 00:47:24.820
If you're planning to stay for
more than a year,

00:47:25.120 --> 00:47:26.755
you'll have to join
the Women's Association.

00:47:27.856 --> 00:47:28.890
I'm sorry.

00:47:29.524 --> 00:47:31.493
I think we'll be going back before then.

00:47:34.529 --> 00:47:35.964
Is that so?

00:47:37.299 --> 00:47:38.900
All right then.

00:47:39.735 --> 00:47:41.603
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

00:47:43.972 --> 00:47:45.474
She didn't even offer us a glass of water.

00:47:46.274 --> 00:47:47.442
That's just wrong.

00:47:47.442 --> 00:47:48.477
Forget it.

00:47:48.477 --> 00:47:50.479
It's not like we don't have
water to drink.

00:47:50.779 --> 00:47:54.649
If you say that, people will say
we're hazing her.

00:47:55.684 --> 00:47:56.985
This is upsetting.

00:48:00.222 --> 00:48:01.223
Unbelievable.

00:48:02.691 --> 00:48:04.860
This is real hazing.

00:48:20.776 --> 00:48:22.511
It doesn't look that difficult.

00:48:25.047 --> 00:48:26.214
Do I just pick it?

00:48:29.584 --> 00:48:30.452
Ow, that hurts.

00:48:34.723 --> 00:48:37.025
What? How am I supposed to do this?

00:48:37.325 --> 00:48:38.326
It hurts so much.

00:48:52.941 --> 00:48:55.043
What was that?
Something just went past me.

00:49:08.590 --> 00:49:09.658
What was that?

00:49:11.593 --> 00:49:12.461
What?

00:49:13.462 --> 00:49:14.362
Ma'am.

00:49:15.130 --> 00:49:17.365
How do you pick them so easily?

00:49:18.767 --> 00:49:19.735
Ma'am.

00:49:21.203 --> 00:49:22.137
Did she not hear me?

00:49:37.252 --> 00:49:39.588
Ma'am. I'll come over to your side.

00:49:43.658 --> 00:49:44.960
Ma'am.

00:49:50.399 --> 00:49:52.100
A hearing aid.

00:49:53.435 --> 00:49:55.370
I guess you can't hear very well.

00:49:56.104 --> 00:49:59.274
I'll watch and learn from you.

00:50:08.116 --> 00:50:09.084
I'm sorry.

00:50:52.260 --> 00:50:53.228
Who?

00:50:54.496 --> 00:50:56.965
You're the scooter girl from earlier.

00:50:58.066 --> 00:50:59.735
Oh.

00:51:00.268 --> 00:51:03.338
He's from the family that moved here
from Seoul.

00:51:03.338 --> 00:51:04.506
And this girl...

00:51:04.506 --> 00:51:06.241
She lives next door to yours.

00:51:06.241 --> 00:51:07.876
You two are neighbors.

00:51:12.714 --> 00:51:14.015
The phone guy.

00:51:15.684 --> 00:51:17.753
So what happened to your clothes?

00:51:22.824 --> 00:51:23.592
Well...

00:51:23.592 --> 00:51:26.128
He looked bored, rolling around
in the field. So we brought him here.

00:51:26.695 --> 00:51:29.765
Hey, tall boy. You know what'll happen
if you don't fill that basket, right?

00:51:29.765 --> 00:51:31.433
I'll smack you.

00:51:31.433 --> 00:51:32.868
I can do a good job.

00:51:33.702 --> 00:51:34.669
I'll do my best.

00:51:38.240 --> 00:51:39.074
Ow.

00:51:39.307 --> 00:51:41.843
- He's useless.
- Goodness.

00:51:48.083 --> 00:51:50.952
You've clearly never touched dirt
in your whole life.

00:51:51.720 --> 00:51:52.854
Are you a student?

00:51:52.854 --> 00:51:54.222
Yes, I'm a college student.

00:51:55.157 --> 00:51:57.759
I came down here for a bit with my dad.

00:51:58.794 --> 00:52:01.063
A college student came here with his dad.

00:52:01.063 --> 00:52:02.497
You're a good son.

00:52:02.497 --> 00:52:03.865
I'm only staying a few days.

00:52:05.033 --> 00:52:06.868
Oh. I'm Im Bo Mi.

00:52:06.868 --> 00:52:08.303
I'm a nutritionist at a school here.

00:52:08.303 --> 00:52:11.073
I come and help out in the fields
like this when I have free time.

00:52:11.473 --> 00:52:13.742
I'm Seong Ji Cheon.

00:52:30.192 --> 00:52:32.761
Right here.
You have to grab the top part here.

00:52:33.228 --> 00:52:34.529
Cucumber thorns are sharp,

00:52:34.529 --> 00:52:36.198
so even with gloves, it hurts
if you grab too hard.

00:52:40.001 --> 00:52:41.036
Like this?

00:52:41.036 --> 00:52:42.471
Like this. Like this.

00:52:54.549 --> 00:52:56.218
This is where the future begins.

00:52:57.953 --> 00:52:59.187
Seong Tae Hun napa cabbage.

00:53:00.355 --> 00:53:02.524
Kimchi made
from multi-functional cabbage...

00:53:05.193 --> 00:53:07.462
that tastes good and
has anti-cancer properties.

00:53:23.378 --> 00:53:24.579
(Napa cabbage variety development
fully suspended)

00:53:45.067 --> 00:53:47.069
(Seedling greenhouse)

00:53:52.641 --> 00:53:55.510
(Yeonri-ri Project)

00:53:56.178 --> 00:53:57.412
Farming isn't complicated.

00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:01.083
All I need is land, seeds, and water.

00:54:01.083 --> 00:54:02.084
I have everything here.

00:54:03.385 --> 00:54:05.887
If you plant it, it'll grow.

00:54:12.394 --> 00:54:15.530
If you plant it, it'll grow.

00:54:25.707 --> 00:54:28.410
Why isn't this working? Why?

00:54:28.410 --> 00:54:31.012
Why won't it work? Why? Why? Why?

00:54:31.012 --> 00:54:34.449
It's working. It's working.

00:54:44.659 --> 00:54:45.527
It's working.

00:54:46.094 --> 00:54:48.063
It's working. It's working. It's working.

00:55:15.023 --> 00:55:17.826
Yes. I can do this.

00:55:17.826 --> 00:55:20.362
I will go back to Seoul...

00:55:20.362 --> 00:55:22.631
with my wife and kids!

00:55:23.432 --> 00:55:26.802
I'm going back.

00:55:28.103 --> 00:55:30.772
You seem full of energy.
What are you doing here?

00:55:31.473 --> 00:55:33.942
Chief. I'm farming.

00:55:34.843 --> 00:55:37.679
This isn't even your own plot.

00:55:37.979 --> 00:55:39.815
You got demoted so this is your hobby now?

00:55:41.149 --> 00:55:43.685
I wasn't demoted.

00:55:44.453 --> 00:55:45.987
I understand why you think that,

00:55:45.987 --> 00:55:48.657
but I came here to develop napa cabbage...

00:55:48.657 --> 00:55:50.292
that only Mat Story can produce.

00:55:50.726 --> 00:55:51.560
Napa cabbage?

00:55:53.128 --> 00:55:54.129
Napa cabbage farming?

00:55:54.663 --> 00:55:55.697
Yes.

00:55:55.697 --> 00:55:57.032
Napa cabbage with consistent sugar levels,

00:55:57.032 --> 00:55:58.867
and specialized nutrients,

00:55:58.867 --> 00:56:00.368
grown organically,

00:56:00.368 --> 00:56:02.204
and made into a specialty product
of Yeonri-ri...

00:56:02.204 --> 00:56:05.340
So Mat Story napa cabbage will
become a local specialty?

00:56:05.674 --> 00:56:07.943
Yes, exactly.

00:56:08.210 --> 00:56:10.278
I'll call it Seong Tae Hun cabbage...

00:56:10.278 --> 00:56:11.346
Have...

00:56:12.814 --> 00:56:14.483
Have some shame.

00:56:14.483 --> 00:56:16.952
You're basically a slave
to a big corporation, aren't you?

00:56:16.952 --> 00:56:17.986
Chief.

00:56:18.387 --> 00:56:20.055
That's a bit harsh, don't you think?

00:56:20.055 --> 00:56:21.223
Harsh?

00:56:21.890 --> 00:56:24.092
You showed up looking like a beggar
in this heat,

00:56:24.092 --> 00:56:26.661
so I even helped you find a house,

00:56:26.661 --> 00:56:28.063
and now listen to the nonsense
you're spouting.

00:56:28.663 --> 00:56:31.600
I was going to let it go because
I made mistakes, too,

00:56:31.600 --> 00:56:34.336
but do you even have
a real estate license?

00:56:34.336 --> 00:56:36.271
Showing houses without a license...

00:56:36.271 --> 00:56:37.839
is fraud.

00:56:37.839 --> 00:56:39.508
A real estate license?
I'm glad you mentioned it.

00:56:39.508 --> 00:56:41.576
What about you?
Do you have a farming license?

00:56:42.344 --> 00:56:44.746
Why would I need a license to farm?

00:56:44.746 --> 00:56:46.448
Yes, you do.

00:56:47.049 --> 00:56:49.351
Because farming is something
done by people.

00:56:49.684 --> 00:56:51.987
But Mat Story isn't people.

00:56:51.987 --> 00:56:54.056
It's a beast that killed this land.

00:56:54.623 --> 00:56:56.958
How can you say this land is dead?

00:56:58.326 --> 00:57:01.229
You left this fine land abandoned for
ten years and killed it.

00:57:01.630 --> 00:57:04.099
Clear away the rocks if you want.
See if a blade of grass will grow.

00:57:04.099 --> 00:57:06.968
I used to be a researcher.
I know what to do.

00:57:06.968 --> 00:57:08.670
No, you don't.

00:57:09.304 --> 00:57:11.940
I'll make sure you can't do anything here.

00:57:12.441 --> 00:57:14.376
That's ridiculous.

00:57:14.376 --> 00:57:15.811
How can you possibly do that?

00:57:18.046 --> 00:57:18.980
Tell me.

00:57:19.448 --> 00:57:20.482
What do you think...

00:57:20.949 --> 00:57:22.017
you can do on your own here...

00:57:22.451 --> 00:57:23.719
without me?

00:57:53.115 --> 00:57:54.383
Village...

00:57:55.751 --> 00:57:57.085
chief!

00:58:39.327 --> 00:58:42.898
Like being struck by lightning
and splashed with water.

00:58:42.898 --> 00:58:43.732
Yes.

00:58:44.299 --> 00:58:45.667
That could happen in life.

00:58:46.301 --> 00:58:47.869
It happens.

00:58:47.869 --> 00:58:52.240
But why does it have to be me?

00:59:02.017 --> 00:59:04.453
(We thank Min Sung Wuk
for his special appearance)

00:59:25.640 --> 00:59:28.643
(Cabbage Your Life)

00:59:28.643 --> 00:59:32.080
Send 1,500 seedling samples
within a month.

00:59:33.448 --> 00:59:35.450
Why won't it grow? Why?

00:59:36.284 --> 00:59:38.453
Mr. Seong Ji Cheon.

00:59:39.121 --> 00:59:40.322
I'm Officer Park Soon Kyung.

00:59:40.322 --> 00:59:41.256
Easy to remember, right?

00:59:43.158 --> 00:59:45.193
I officially declare this
as the village chief.

00:59:45.193 --> 00:59:47.896
Do not help Seong Tae Hun at all.

00:59:47.896 --> 00:59:49.431
Village chief's official stamp.

00:59:49.431 --> 00:59:50.832
Get a recommendation from
the village chief.

00:59:50.832 --> 00:59:53.001
Village chief. Village chief.
Village chief.

00:59:53.001 --> 00:59:55.437
I'll deal with
the Women's Association first.

00:59:55.437 --> 00:59:56.772
Hello.

00:59:57.406 --> 00:59:58.607
Let's find a way.

00:59:58.607 --> 01:00:00.375
If there's no proper way,
I'll find another way.

01:00:03.445 --> 01:00:05.447
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)